[{:db/id "q-24575/selection/d75fb5723a0e137e3747d2aa5e777ff50c94c94bd878e904298b1d4c37466d49" :answer/id #uuid "e55f241a-779f-5e97-b1b7-f13353144ee3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24575/selection/0eec57f836554a465e83a2333137ef1566a186d658c30e3a214e0e7734da1d12" :answer/id #uuid "f94cb9c0-1aef-5920-9e36-292ab6763aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24575/selection/8bcbfec71e5682026371e8e007f9ce548e4de141af4bb9a30130cdb322c4da4a" :answer/id #uuid "e997ce2d-a1d4-59a7-b20d-754d3ed14510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=7(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24575/selection/917148de2965dac2bb0f54fa06e902c39fe034ba95a9e42f612b2814cfd21f8c" :answer/id #uuid "c541779d-bbe7-5c87-8f30-1ed1b67ea24f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24575/selection/fffb6e78a72034da06c266f49ccce6846f674ae764587a44c4abe1493fe2594f" :answer/id #uuid "ca950cea-4977-5929-b108-f1f297fada93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24575/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d956d25-b226-5c60-804c-520274c8dd5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-24575/selection/917148de2965dac2bb0f54fa06e902c39fe034ba95a9e42f612b2814cfd21f8c" :answer-field/choices ["q-24575/selection/d75fb5723a0e137e3747d2aa5e777ff50c94c94bd878e904298b1d4c37466d49" "q-24575/selection/0eec57f836554a465e83a2333137ef1566a186d658c30e3a214e0e7734da1d12" "q-24575/selection/8bcbfec71e5682026371e8e007f9ce548e4de141af4bb9a30130cdb322c4da4a" "q-24575/selection/917148de2965dac2bb0f54fa06e902c39fe034ba95a9e42f612b2814cfd21f8c" "q-24575/selection/fffb6e78a72034da06c266f49ccce6846f674ae764587a44c4abe1493fe2594f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-24575" :question/id #uuid "a1295497-95f0-563c-9b4d-4d497affdde7" :question/math-academy-id "q-24575" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\frac{x}{3} \\\\ y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\frac{x}{3}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{4}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{4} & =2{(-\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{4} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1 \\\\ y & =4(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=4(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-24575/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78dbecb4-68d4-53b0-b47f-f37ce92da896"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-24575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664/selection/a0c1bea34cee0c467de1aff242ec6a0d057f15ef7391acdf349364e63e035bf1" :answer/id #uuid "f82d2a4d-807f-5a5c-93fa-f6f20429dd11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)^{2}(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664/selection/0b5f8c1d22c8d64b3b3e54e2664844ef4bbe0f5d6e4fb6a9a0f5ad7b338aa8d3" :answer/id #uuid "ceee72aa-ee31-5323-8443-523f2234a0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}(x+3)^{2}(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664/selection/cdd3227a7d39a609bd3d6d3cacb44c421a294af2b88eba1d49b24526f9d49707" :answer/id #uuid "c4a63922-2589-5ebc-bba0-9c8f77371341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+3)^{2}(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664/selection/81a044786f6a5e2b6f936da5a9404c52c22e63539836d0905e84ad70ad3fba8c" :answer/id #uuid "2c47a2dc-1e64-54ee-9a80-14d0dca49ca9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664/selection/354ff1308473368ffef52e28fce037e473c7d45ea271f6e26fd2018caa51cf3d" :answer/id #uuid "8452cb91-7694-52d5-a8f7-64a61f1c102c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{4}(x+3)(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be0e7474-ddca-5d74-85f5-84048b123a20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102664/selection/a0c1bea34cee0c467de1aff242ec6a0d057f15ef7391acdf349364e63e035bf1" :answer-field/choices ["q-102664/selection/a0c1bea34cee0c467de1aff242ec6a0d057f15ef7391acdf349364e63e035bf1" "q-102664/selection/0b5f8c1d22c8d64b3b3e54e2664844ef4bbe0f5d6e4fb6a9a0f5ad7b338aa8d3" "q-102664/selection/cdd3227a7d39a609bd3d6d3cacb44c421a294af2b88eba1d49b24526f9d49707" "q-102664/selection/81a044786f6a5e2b6f936da5a9404c52c22e63539836d0905e84ad70ad3fba8c" "q-102664/selection/354ff1308473368ffef52e28fce037e473c7d45ea271f6e26fd2018caa51cf3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102664" :question/id #uuid "9907e86a-7f0e-52ec-b8f3-600094230c4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102664" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=1-2t,\\,\\,\\,y=(t-2)^{2}(t+1),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1-2t\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{1-x}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{1-x}{2}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{1-x}{2}-2)}^{2}(\\frac{1-x}{2}+1) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1-x-4}{2})}^{2}(\\frac{1-x+2}{2}) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-x-3}{2})}^{2}(\\frac{3-x}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)^{2}(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=-\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)^{2}(x-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102664/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79107609-77e6-55e9-970d-da63c39daf0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102664"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320926/field-1/b113e2a3bfd65a5e4c301f6d0ea67b93cc11ee524f25c93ce024922cdff210c9" :answer/id #uuid "3fedd790-b414-5df0-b803-c6a6e192da48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320926/field-1/cd3343b72b1f50cb8b0a4142afb1ebc33afe7297eb631de0cc85d126107af057" :answer/id #uuid "48722a34-c240-5044-91ab-55900841e87d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-3x}{7x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320926/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a9c97f1-891e-564f-8f1f-38428b9f0bd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320926/field-1/b113e2a3bfd65a5e4c301f6d0ea67b93cc11ee524f25c93ce024922cdff210c9" :answer-field/choices ["q-320926/field-1/b113e2a3bfd65a5e4c301f6d0ea67b93cc11ee524f25c93ce024922cdff210c9" "q-320926/field-1/cd3343b72b1f50cb8b0a4142afb1ebc33afe7297eb631de0cc85d126107af057"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320926/field-2/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer/id #uuid "db7f0568-4682-57f4-ac6a-4e4e92a2b0ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320926/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "741bd4b4-b682-5c8d-82e9-5875f1a98167" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320926/field-2/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer-field/choices ["q-320926/field-2/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320926" :question/id #uuid "68b75bd8-3590-5aaa-ab0b-d5ba8601a2b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-320926" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{t}{-2t+1},\\,t\\ne -3,\\,\\,\\,t\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ne $\n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t+3}\\,⇒\\,t=-3+\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=-3+\\frac{1}{x}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-3+\\frac{1}{x})}{(-2\\,(-3+\\frac{1}{x})+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3+\\frac{1}{x})}{(6-\\frac{2}{x}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3+\\frac{1}{x})}{(7-\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3x+1}{\\cancel{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{x}}{7x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2}.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ne \\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{1}{t+3}$ has range $x\\ne 0,$ we must have \n$x\\ne \\frac{2}{7},\\text{ }0.$ \n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2},\\,x\\ne \\frac{2}{7},\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-320926/field-1" "q-320926/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79107609-77e6-55e9-970d-da63c39daf0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320946/field-1/4045dbc1ddbc0b09527fef32ab24de5983af068a516010fed310098a24d511d6" :answer/id #uuid "b2d7fdfb-7593-576b-95d5-708df9d988cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{9}+(y+2)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320946/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce949294-a5bb-59b8-b616-d52224c4ba47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320946/field-1/4045dbc1ddbc0b09527fef32ab24de5983af068a516010fed310098a24d511d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-320946/field-1/4045dbc1ddbc0b09527fef32ab24de5983af068a516010fed310098a24d511d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320946" :question/id #uuid "bc324745-12fd-530c-8527-373071b9f1c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320946" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n{{field-1}}$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{3} \\\\ y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320946/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78dbecb4-68d4-53b0-b47f-f37ce92da896"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
